the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a person* may make a will.
    *a person* is a person; scenario element.
    *a person* is *a number* years of age; scenario element.
    *a person* is an active military member; scenario element.

the knowledge base wills includes:

the text of the Wills Act is at "sources/wills.md".

the text of the Blawx project is at "sources/wills.yaml".

% The Act, section by section.
rule section_1 with provenance the Wills Act at section 1:
a person may make a will if
    the person is a person
    and the person is a number N years of age
    and N >= 18.

rule section_2 with provenance the Wills Act at section 2:
a person may make a will if
    the person is a person
    and the person is an active military member
    and the person is a number N years of age
    and N >= 14.

scenario valid_will is, as stated in the Blawx project at test valid_will:
    valid_will expects answers [].

scenario case_1 is, as stated in the case analysis of the encoding at section 1:
    % a case of the rule of section 1 (blawx_cases.pl), answered by Blawx
    person_a is a person.
    person_a is 18 years of age.
    which_may_make_a_will expects answers ["person_a may make a will"].

